# netsurf: Vita diagnostics mirrored to the PC over UDP (frontends/vita)
# Generated 2026-09-23
#
# The on-device plot-stream log that doc 03 anticipated, and a fix for the
# results transfer: hardware run 2's copies were stale (Explorer's FTP
# cache) and runs 4 and 5 never reached the results folder.
# - netlog.c/.h (new): everything written under ux0:data/VitaBrowser/ --
#   log.txt, netsurf.log, the plot dumps, autotest.done -- is also sent over
#   UDP as it is written, to a receiver on the LAN (VitaBrowser repo:
#   tools/vita-netlog.py) that rebuilds the same files per launch. Broadcast
#   until the receiver answers, then unicast; sequence numbers for losses;
#   each finished file carries its length and CRC-32. Non-blocking, paced
#   (2 ms per ~10 KB), pauses itself when the network is gone; never fatal.
#   Plain BSD sockets (vitaSDK newlib on sceNet), so the simulator runs the
#   same code. netlog.cfg: "off" or "a.b.c.d[:port]".
# - diag.c: log.txt lines mirrored live (held until the network is up),
#   netsurf.log tailed about once a second, dumps and markers sent when
#   closed, end marks at autotest.done and exit, counters in the log.
# - main.c: start after the engine log, report at autotest end, stop at
#   exit; AUTOTEST DONE names the receiver the results went to.
# - Makefile: netlog.c; SceNet / SceNetCtl stubs.
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 6.

